XR presentation: the diorama's frames (head pose tag, stretched eyes) and a general eye shift

For WakerQuest's diorama (native/src/pc/game_hooks/pc_vr_diorama.cpp, android/xr/wq_xr.cpp), which
draws the world for the headset's eyes through the view delta (patch 0019):
- aurora_xr_set_frame_info(tag, diorama), from the game thread while it records a frame: taken by
  the frame's present and published with it (AuroraXrFrame.tag, .diorama), so the XR layer shows the
  frame as a projection layer for the head pose it was drawn for. A diorama frame's eyes are the EFB
  stretched over each half of the buffer (as wide as the EFB, no 4:3 letterbox).
- The eyes' shift (patch 0024) becomes clip.x += eye * (a * clip.w + b), set with
  aurora_xr_set_eye_shift(enable, a, b); aurora_xr_set_stereo(strength, focus) is a = strength,
  b = -strength * focus. The immediate word carries a and sign(b) * sqrt(|b| / 64) as two snorm16,
  so the screen's focus term (several clip units) and the diorama's eye offset (hundredths) both keep
  their precision.

